WEBVTT

00:24:56.290 --> 00:25:00.758
but I'm curious from your surveying
of companies and founders and CEOs,

00:25:00.782 --> 00:25:02.682
if you've seen that as a common trait?

00:25:03.946 --> 00:25:05.611
AG: Yeah, I think so.

00:25:05.635 --> 00:25:08.322
There's evidence that charismatic leaders

00:25:08.346 --> 00:25:11.615
are more successful at pitching
their companies and fundraising.

00:25:12.108 --> 00:25:15.239
It's not surprising, I think,
to anyone that that would be true.

00:25:15.858 --> 00:25:19.067
There is also evidence
that the cultural blueprints

00:25:19.091 --> 00:25:20.702
that founders have in their minds

00:25:20.726 --> 00:25:23.107
when they first launched their companies,

00:25:23.131 --> 00:25:26.234
they cast a real shadow
on the future of the company,

00:25:26.258 --> 00:25:29.091
even if founders rotate out of leadership.

00:25:29.581 --> 00:25:33.232
There's a study of a couple a hundred
Silicon Valley start-ups